From 95fd7922ac9f04c9c6e09e9239c8912a57e27718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:00:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, 840D and Doosan DNM state the
 mm unit before any motion

These five mill posts always write millimetre numbers but wrote no unit
word, so a control left in inch by power-on or the last program read
every coordinate 25.4x too long. Each now states the unit it writes in
its opening block: G21 in a block of its own at the end of onOpen
(Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM), and G710 (metric lengths and feeds)
in the 840D's section opening block, so its N numbering is unchanged.

The posts do not read machine.units and refuse nothing: where the
program's unit is chosen, and inch output, is #902 (maintainer scope
change on the issue). Goldens change only by the new word; the
macro_b probe reader models G21; regression line counts +1.

Pinned by post_unit_word (one test per post).

Fixes #901

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
